WEBVTT


00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.192
My flight was cancelled.


00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:41.193
Fuck.


00:02:41.259 --> 00:02:42.460
Yeah. We're fogged in.


00:02:42.526 --> 00:02:43.793
Well, where are you?


00:02:43.859 --> 00:02:46.127
Still at the airport, obviously.


00:02:46.192 --> 00:02:47.793
Well, Laurent says it's sunny at home.


00:02:47.859 --> 00:02:50.127
l don't know what to tell you, Laura.


00:02:50.192 --> 00:02:53.028
l can come in tomorrow or the next day.


00:02:53.093 --> 00:02:54.461
Absolutely not, Jayne.


00:02:54.526 --> 00:02:57.061
l have been stuck out here for a week
taking care of him,


00:02:57.126 --> 00:02:58.494
l've got to get back to San Francisco.


00:02:58.559 --> 00:03:00.227
So you keep saying. Slower.


00:03:00.292 --> 00:03:01.760
l'm sorry, Miss. We can't drive this slow.


00:03:01.826 --> 00:03:03.327
We're going to get pulled over.


00:03:03.392 --> 00:03:07.596
No. l don't care if you have to charter
a plane to Pittsburgh. You can amord it.


00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:08.926
lt's there.


00:03:08.993 --> 00:03:11.328
Some of us have to actually work
for a living.


00:03:11.392 --> 00:03:12.326
Stop. Stop.


00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:15.762
- What?
- Stop.


00:03:15.826 --> 00:03:19.896
Stop pressuring me.


00:03:21.292 --> 00:03:23.027
l'll be there, and when l get there,


00:03:23.093 --> 00:03:24.761
l'm going to prove you wrong, okay?


00:03:24.826 --> 00:03:28.262
- Get your ass here because l'm--
- The fog is lifting.


00:03:28.325 --> 00:03:29.626
No! l--


00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.762
Take a stroll.


00:03:40.826 --> 00:03:42.160
Go on.


00:03:51.659 --> 00:03:53.193
How do you love them?


00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:00.660
l can't believe these are my legs.


00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:05.695
Quite reasonable at 2,800.


00:04:15.993 --> 00:04:17.394
So which do you prefer?


00:04:18.492 --> 00:04:20.694
The black or the blue?


00:04:22.826 --> 00:04:25.562
The boot on your right foot is blue--


00:04:25.626 --> 00:04:29.363
nearly imperceptibly blue.


00:04:29.425 --> 00:04:31.627
You can't stare at it, though.


00:04:32.826 --> 00:04:34.494
You look, then look away.


00:05:10.826 --> 00:05:13.929
So...who is it?


00:05:13.993 --> 00:05:16.095
Who's the artist?


00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.361
Milton Hofsteder.


00:05:19.659 --> 00:05:20.793
l've heard of him.


00:05:22.993 --> 00:05:25.762
l think l just read something about him.


00:05:25.826 --> 00:05:27.294
An obituary.


00:05:29.492 --> 00:05:30.492
Yeah.


00:05:33.492 --> 00:05:34.826
Couple of months ago.


00:05:37.659 --> 00:05:38.726
Have you been inside?


00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.227
Would you buckle my shoe?


00:05:53.826 --> 00:05:55.027
Jackson.


00:05:55.093 --> 00:05:56.761
Here's the son.


00:05:56.826 --> 00:05:59.695
Hey. Crazy timing, right?


00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.561
But the work looks so powerful.


00:06:02.626 --> 00:06:05.762
Your dad would have been happy, right?


00:06:05.826 --> 00:06:08.128
Just wish he could have been here.


00:06:08.192 --> 00:06:09.893
Just remember, l've got a great stam,


00:06:09.959 --> 00:06:12.561
and you can hand it over to us
any time you want.


00:06:12.626 --> 00:06:14.094
Don't go.


00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.430
l'm Eli. l'm sorry, this is---


00:06:18.492 --> 00:06:19.826
Mrs. Hofsteder?


00:06:27.826 --> 00:06:29.160
Mrs. Hofsteder?


00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:35.059
Mrs. Hofsteder?


00:06:38.826 --> 00:06:40.861
Mrs. Hofsteder?


00:06:40.926 --> 00:06:42.627
We're about to make our final descent.


00:06:44.826 --> 00:06:46.394
Final descent?


00:06:46.459 --> 00:06:48.093
We're about to land in Pittsburgh.


00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.394
May l take this?


00:06:50.826 --> 00:06:52.160
Take what?


00:06:52.225 --> 00:06:53.826
Your cocMail.


00:06:53.893 --> 00:06:55.327
l don't drink.


00:06:55.392 --> 00:06:57.927
l'll just take it, then.


00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.095
Do you mind
changing this station?


00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.095
Thank you.


00:07:44.492 --> 00:07:45.593
Could you change it again?


00:07:47.492 --> 00:07:49.093
Could you change it again?


00:08:42.325 --> 00:08:44.560
Laura?


00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:47.659
Daddy?


00:08:53.826 --> 00:08:54.826
Laura!


00:08:59.492 --> 00:09:00.659
Laura!


00:09:10.659 --> 00:09:11.659
Thanks a lot.


00:09:13.325 --> 00:09:15.760
So don't pack 20 changes of clothes.


00:09:15.826 --> 00:09:18.495
l packed your stum, too.
Your place was such a mess.


00:09:18.559 --> 00:09:19.760
A sweater and a folder.


00:09:19.826 --> 00:09:21.761
Well...


00:09:21.826 --> 00:09:24.428
lf you have a couple of kids and no help--


00:09:24.492 --> 00:09:28.095
Okay. Hi.


00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.094
Good to see you.


00:09:31.993 --> 00:09:34.095
New?


00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:35.327
Yeah.


00:09:39.826 --> 00:09:42.094
They're...they're boots.


00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:43.261
Nice.


00:09:43.325 --> 00:09:44.426
Yeah?


00:09:44.492 --> 00:09:45.893
- They're blue.
- Black.


00:09:45.959 --> 00:09:47.260
No, they're blue.


00:09:47.325 --> 00:09:48.759
l guarantee you, they're black.


00:09:48.826 --> 00:09:51.662
No, they're blue in the daylight.
You'll see.


00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.427
What did you do to your face?


00:09:54.492 --> 00:09:55.759
Nothing. But you look good.


00:09:55.826 --> 00:09:57.761
No, l look like shit, and yes, you did.


00:09:57.826 --> 00:09:59.093
l've only been gone for a week.


00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.761
What could l have done in a week?


00:10:00.826 --> 00:10:03.361
l really wouldn't know.
l'm not up on it.


00:10:03.425 --> 00:10:05.760
l don't know what to tell you.


00:10:05.826 --> 00:10:08.595
So where's Daddy?
Where's the patient?


00:10:08.659 --> 00:10:10.093
Where's my folder?


00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.361
lt's in the thing.


00:10:11.425 --> 00:10:13.160
Daddy.


00:10:13.225 --> 00:10:15.894
Sugar lip baby. How you doing?


00:10:15.959 --> 00:10:17.894
- Good.
- Firm and trim,


00:10:17.959 --> 00:10:20.895
but you can't lie still long enough
to get pregnant,


00:10:20.959 --> 00:10:22.894
- can you?
- That's right.


00:10:24.893 --> 00:10:27.095
So Laura says you're acting strange.


00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.227
l'm just fine.


00:10:28.292 --> 00:10:30.427
Well, you look fine. Told you.


00:10:30.492 --> 00:10:31.759
Yeah.


00:10:31.826 --> 00:10:33.427
What happened to your shirt, Joe?


00:10:33.492 --> 00:10:35.393
l puked on it.


00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:42.061
- Are you okay?
- Well, why not?


00:10:42.126 --> 00:10:46.930
l got a house full of beautiful chicks
and a backyard full of gold.


00:10:46.993 --> 00:10:48.427
What else can a man want?


00:10:48.492 --> 00:10:50.727
Except maybe a little head now and then.


00:10:50.792 --> 00:10:53.761
Oh, Daddy.


00:10:53.826 --> 00:10:55.594
Aren't you a little too old for that?


00:10:55.659 --> 00:10:57.594
You better ask my lady friend.


00:10:57.659 --> 00:10:59.494
No, thank you.


00:11:08.826 --> 00:11:12.095
We don't have to worry
about you, do we?


00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:13.761
No.


00:11:13.826 --> 00:11:18.096
That phone call last week
gave me a little scare.


00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:20.362
You were a little confused.


00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:26.864
l talked on the phone
to Laura last week, not you.


00:11:26.926 --> 00:11:28.060
Yeah, but--


00:11:28.126 --> 00:11:32.096
Seems to me you are the one
who's a little confused.


00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:36.128
Joe, do you have to go to the bathroom?


00:11:36.192 --> 00:11:37.760
She's got a thing
about my bowel movements.


00:11:37.826 --> 00:11:39.194
Yeah.


00:11:39.259 --> 00:11:42.762
l thought you were here to relieve me.


00:11:42.826 --> 00:11:45.261
She says you're the one that's strange.


00:11:47.792 --> 00:11:49.860
Poor Woofie.


00:11:49.926 --> 00:11:53.429
l know. Couldn't survive without Mommy,
unlike some people.


00:11:56.659 --> 00:11:59.428
So tell me about your new lady friend.


00:11:59.492 --> 00:12:02.428
She's a mother fucker.


00:12:02.492 --> 00:12:04.760
Can't wait to meet her.


00:12:04.826 --> 00:12:06.160
Shelly's her name.


00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:08.427
She's something else.


00:12:08.492 --> 00:12:10.093
She's a nurse.


00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.828
She sure is.


00:12:13.292 --> 00:12:14.760
Go get him a shirt.


00:12:14.826 --> 00:12:16.627
The pile on the couch is clean.


00:12:23.492 --> 00:12:24.492
Hey--


00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.227
You're Shelly.


00:12:31.492 --> 00:12:32.960
l'm late for work.


00:12:40.659 --> 00:12:42.761
Don't give me a hard time. Come on.


00:12:42.826 --> 00:12:44.761
No.


00:12:44.826 --> 00:12:45.826
Drink.


00:12:48.492 --> 00:12:51.428
Just take it. Don't be a baby.


00:12:51.492 --> 00:12:52.759
Blood pressure.


00:12:52.826 --> 00:12:55.094
She's wearing Mommy's good coat.


00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.095
Here's his meds for next week.


00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:00.396
Phone numbers, what to do when,
where, et cetera, et cetera.


00:13:03.826 --> 00:13:08.230
Why don't you dig up that treasure
and buy that nurse a new car?


00:13:08.292 --> 00:13:10.694
Because l'm going to leave that
for you girls after l die.


00:13:12.292 --> 00:13:14.060
All right, come on.


00:13:16.225 --> 00:13:17.759
Joe!


00:13:17.826 --> 00:13:21.863
Joe, l just asked you
if you had to go to the bathroom.


00:13:21.926 --> 00:13:23.761
Oh, God. Take it out of here.


00:13:23.826 --> 00:13:25.928
Oh, Daddy.


00:13:25.993 --> 00:13:27.861
Come on. Let's go.


00:13:27.926 --> 00:13:30.762
l asked you to get me diapers
after the last time.


00:13:30.826 --> 00:13:32.594
Come on. Get a move on.


00:13:32.659 --> 00:13:33.926
That means you, too.


00:13:33.993 --> 00:13:37.596
Hold it, Omicer.
You got the wrong man.


00:13:37.659 --> 00:13:39.127
Can you just be still?


00:13:39.192 --> 00:13:41.861
Let's pull them down, all right?


00:13:41.926 --> 00:13:44.194
You better get used to it


00:13:44.259 --> 00:13:45.727
because l'm out of here
day after tomorrow.


00:13:45.792 --> 00:13:46.859
You got the wrong man.


00:13:46.926 --> 00:13:48.060
Yeah, very funny, Joe.


00:13:48.126 --> 00:13:49.527
We got it the first time.


00:13:49.592 --> 00:13:51.593
- Let's go to the park.
- Let's go play in the park.


00:13:51.659 --> 00:13:53.093
l want to go inside and see Daddy.


00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:54.427
Come on, this is your favorite ball.


00:13:54.492 --> 00:13:55.759
You love to play with it.


00:13:55.826 --> 00:13:58.094
He's inside the house.


00:13:58.160 --> 00:13:59.761
No, come on. Let's go to the park.


00:13:59.826 --> 00:14:03.629
Here, you can carry
the ball to the park.


00:14:06.492 --> 00:14:09.261
Not with your hands, Jayne.


00:14:09.325 --> 00:14:11.226
Are you crazy? That's disgusting.


00:14:11.292 --> 00:14:12.626
What's wrong with you?


00:14:12.692 --> 00:14:15.728
Here, look, just get me some liquid soap
from under the sink.


00:14:15.792 --> 00:14:16.926
That's cold.


00:14:16.993 --> 00:14:18.761
Jesus Christ.


00:14:20.026 --> 00:14:22.094
Strawberry. Remember this smell?


00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:24.462
Just get over here.
Do you want this to take all night?


00:14:24.526 --> 00:14:26.227
Whoever used this shit?


00:14:26.292 --> 00:14:27.226
l'm not talking to you.


00:14:27.292 --> 00:14:29.894
Wow, wow, wow.


00:14:33.492 --> 00:14:34.826
Damn it.


00:14:38.792 --> 00:14:39.959
Damn it.


00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:43.160
Damn it.


00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:48.494
Damn it.


00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:54.161
Damn it.


00:14:56.492 --> 00:14:57.426
Damn it.


00:15:02.659 --> 00:15:04.293
Oh, man.


00:15:06.059 --> 00:15:07.727
- Eli, l don't know what l did with--
- It's me, Jackson.


00:15:07.792 --> 00:15:09.393
Honey, where are you?


00:15:09.459 --> 00:15:10.960
- At Daddy's.
- Already?


00:15:11.026 --> 00:15:12.394
How is he?


00:15:12.459 --> 00:15:13.860
How are you? How was the flight?


00:15:15.492 --> 00:15:16.559
Yeah. The flight was good.


00:15:17.926 --> 00:15:20.428
Sorry. So that's good.


00:15:20.492 --> 00:15:23.161
lt's...


00:15:23.225 --> 00:15:24.759
- Everything's great.
- Good.


00:15:24.826 --> 00:15:26.727
l'm fine, except--


00:15:28.492 --> 00:15:30.760
- It's the FedEx.
- So what? Jackson, listen to me.


00:15:30.826 --> 00:15:32.060
lt's probably from MoMA.


00:15:33.492 --> 00:15:34.893
lt doesn't matter. l'm fine.


00:15:34.959 --> 00:15:37.227
l'm going to have to sign for it. Hold.


00:15:39.492 --> 00:15:43.429
l'm fine, except l just scraped the shit
out of my father's ass-crack


00:15:43.492 --> 00:15:45.160
with my bare hands!


00:15:48.993 --> 00:15:50.027
Om!


00:15:50.093 --> 00:15:52.128
Turn it om!


00:15:53.492 --> 00:15:54.492
Okay.


00:15:58.826 --> 00:16:00.427
What's with this Fort Knox lighting?


00:16:00.492 --> 00:16:02.026
That and this fence.


00:16:02.093 --> 00:16:03.160
lt's like...


00:16:04.359 --> 00:16:09.063
''Attention, robbers.
Lest you pass this dump by,


00:16:09.126 --> 00:16:11.595
let it be known there's
valuable stum in here.''


00:16:11.659 --> 00:16:14.294
Well, he wants people to think
he's got something--


00:16:14.359 --> 00:16:16.427
his buried treasure.


00:16:16.492 --> 00:16:18.493
lt's so counter--


00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:25.194
something.


00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:28.194
l made a plate.


00:16:48.659 --> 00:16:51.428
You didn't tell me he was shitting himself.


00:16:51.492 --> 00:16:53.427
l wanted you to come.


00:16:55.559 --> 00:16:57.160
Yum.


00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.628
l'm so tired.


00:17:05.826 --> 00:17:07.761
Just leave everything to me now.


00:17:09.826 --> 00:17:11.160
lt's not just him.


00:17:11.225 --> 00:17:12.626
lt's...


00:17:12.692 --> 00:17:17.096
work and kids and no money.


00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:18.427
You know, Jackson said--


00:17:18.492 --> 00:17:21.995
We do have a little bit
of pride left, Jayne.


00:17:22.993 --> 00:17:24.994
Well, at least Laurent does.


00:17:27.826 --> 00:17:29.093
No, l quit.


00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.262
l don't drink or smoke anymore.


00:17:31.325 --> 00:17:33.226
Whoa. Really?


00:17:33.292 --> 00:17:38.096
Exercise, diet, and no drugs.


00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.762
Wow. Well, maybe that's going to help.


00:17:40.826 --> 00:17:42.327
Help?


00:17:43.492 --> 00:17:46.428
Oh, that. Yes.


00:17:46.492 --> 00:17:49.328
Plus, l'm going to get my degree.


00:17:51.492 --> 00:17:52.659
Good for you.


00:17:54.492 --> 00:17:57.094
And l'm going to pry Jackson
away from his desk.


00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.861
Yeah. Good luck.


00:18:00.659 --> 00:18:02.494
And get pregnant.


00:18:05.659 --> 00:18:06.659
How much?


00:18:10.325 --> 00:18:12.160
They're 300.


00:18:18.160 --> 00:18:19.094
And change.


00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.327
375.


00:18:22.826 --> 00:18:24.093
On sale.


00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.661
500 plus tax.


00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:33.762
Why do you try to bullshit me?


00:18:39.492 --> 00:18:40.993
Bastard.


00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:45.428
He's got an appointment
with the neurologist in the morning.


00:18:45.492 --> 00:18:46.559
Can you handle it?


00:18:46.626 --> 00:18:48.294
Yeah. That's what l'm here for.


00:18:52.726 --> 00:18:53.860
Right.


00:18:53.926 --> 00:18:55.861
Wait.


00:18:55.926 --> 00:18:57.761
What am l doing here?


00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:37.828
Point.


00:19:37.893 --> 00:19:39.361
Wait.


00:19:41.592 --> 00:19:43.260
Come here.


00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.995
Come here, grimy.


00:20:05.659 --> 00:20:06.760
Are you still doing that?


00:20:08.626 --> 00:20:14.231
Well, l can't tell the dimerence
if mine is open or closed or up, down.


00:20:14.292 --> 00:20:18.429
You have to do it religiously,
every day, so...


00:20:18.492 --> 00:20:22.162
With Laurent, l don't ever have to worry
about missing that crucial day.


00:20:22.225 --> 00:20:24.093
Which l think is coming up for me.


00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:27.096
Yeah? Why don't you
have Jackson come out?


00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.427
He's too busy.


00:20:28.492 --> 00:20:32.429
Not even just for, like,
a little quick wham-bam?


00:20:32.492 --> 00:20:34.594
Take the next flight out.
l mean, he can amord it.


00:20:34.659 --> 00:20:35.760
He's too busy.


00:20:36.759 --> 00:20:38.427
That's your problem.


00:20:38.492 --> 00:20:40.160
With Laurent,
l wouldn't have to ask twice.


00:20:54.826 --> 00:20:57.428
You don't have to go, honey.


00:20:57.492 --> 00:21:00.094
Yes, l do.


00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:01.160
lt's the collectors.


00:21:19.492 --> 00:21:21.093
Jackson!


00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:26.828
- Legacy!
- Father!


00:21:30.492 --> 00:21:32.093
Jackson.


00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:34.095
Whoa!


00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.762
Father.


00:21:36.826 --> 00:21:38.494
Jackson!


00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:41.427
Legacy!


00:21:43.259 --> 00:21:45.227
Father.


00:21:47.492 --> 00:21:49.327
Jackson!


00:21:56.826 --> 00:21:58.594
Father!


00:22:07.659 --> 00:22:08.726
Jackson!


00:22:09.826 --> 00:22:10.826
l love you.


00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:25.429
l would, but the retrospective--


00:22:25.492 --> 00:22:28.428
Please. Just for a night or two.


00:22:28.492 --> 00:22:30.760
l'll make it worth your while.


00:22:30.826 --> 00:22:32.761
The gallery can handle everything,
Jackson.


00:22:32.826 --> 00:22:34.427
l know, but it should be me.


00:22:34.492 --> 00:22:35.759
l know you say that,


00:22:35.826 --> 00:22:37.427
but you know what?


00:22:37.492 --> 00:22:39.460
He didn't appreciate you
when he was alive,


00:22:39.526 --> 00:22:42.095
and he's not around
to appreciate you now.


00:22:42.160 --> 00:22:45.596
You're right, okay?


00:22:45.659 --> 00:22:49.429
But l can't just sit back
and get these proceeds without--


00:22:49.492 --> 00:22:51.827
Without making yourself
miserable in return?


00:22:56.492 --> 00:22:57.726
Okay.


00:22:57.792 --> 00:23:00.427
Really?


00:23:00.492 --> 00:23:02.360
- Yeah.
- Really?


00:23:02.425 --> 00:23:07.530
l'll come. l'll just hop on a plane.


00:23:07.592 --> 00:23:08.759
Okay.


00:23:08.826 --> 00:23:10.761
Plane to Pittsburgh.


00:23:10.826 --> 00:23:11.760
Bye.


00:23:11.826 --> 00:23:12.826
Bye.


00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:21.428
The MRl is fairly conclusive, Jayne.


00:23:21.492 --> 00:23:23.894
That, in combination
with our clinical findings--


00:23:23.959 --> 00:23:26.761
l wish l had better news.


00:23:26.826 --> 00:23:28.127
lt's Binswanger's Disease.


00:23:30.259 --> 00:23:33.095
Binswanger's Disease
is a fairly rare form of dementia.


00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:35.762
There is no specific
course of treatment for it.


00:23:35.826 --> 00:23:37.194
Okay.


00:23:38.325 --> 00:23:39.559
How do we treat it?


00:23:41.492 --> 00:23:44.261
Treatment is symptomatic, l'm afraid.


00:23:44.325 --> 00:23:46.427
Okay.


00:23:46.492 --> 00:23:51.430
Jayne, you need
to prepare yourself for the inevitable.


00:23:51.492 --> 00:23:54.628
Life expectancy for patients
with this condition


00:23:54.692 --> 00:23:56.860
is one year, two at most.


00:23:57.993 --> 00:23:59.060
ln the meantime,


00:23:59.126 --> 00:24:00.560
as his condition deteriorates,


00:24:00.626 --> 00:24:02.794
expect to see...


00:24:07.826 --> 00:24:09.761
...like a facial expression, seizures.


00:24:12.392 --> 00:24:13.526
...cerebral vascular lesion--


00:24:13.592 --> 00:24:15.427
...Die.


00:24:15.492 --> 00:24:16.759
Two years.


00:24:16.826 --> 00:24:18.894
Patients do die within two years,


00:24:18.959 --> 00:24:22.562
but during that time, you can expect
periods of aggression or euphoria--


00:24:22.626 --> 00:24:24.961
Euphoria?


00:24:26.492 --> 00:24:28.327
Possibly, at times.


00:24:29.559 --> 00:24:32.161
ls your sister still in town?


00:24:34.926 --> 00:24:36.027
What the hell is this?


00:24:36.093 --> 00:24:37.360
What's it sliced up like this for?


00:24:37.425 --> 00:24:38.759
lt's teriyaki-style, Dad.


00:24:38.826 --> 00:24:40.427
Teri-- l don't want that.


00:24:40.492 --> 00:24:42.861
- It's cut up. It's plain meat.
- Has that got sauce on it?


00:24:42.926 --> 00:24:44.093
lt's just plain meat.


00:24:44.160 --> 00:24:45.895
Right.


00:24:47.826 --> 00:24:48.826
So?


00:24:50.826 --> 00:24:53.428
Dementia. No cure.


00:24:53.492 --> 00:24:55.493
Two years max.


00:25:04.160 --> 00:25:06.762
How did Mommy ever put up with you?


00:25:08.492 --> 00:25:10.894
Damn if l know.


00:25:12.325 --> 00:25:15.761
Mallory's up in Heaven now.
She knew when to cut out.


00:25:15.826 --> 00:25:17.928
Yep, that's right.


00:25:17.993 --> 00:25:20.995
No woman could ever
measure up after her.


00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:25.428
Right?


00:25:25.492 --> 00:25:28.094
That's a very pretty theory.


00:25:28.160 --> 00:25:30.095
What do you mean?


00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:31.861
You know.


00:25:33.659 --> 00:25:35.761
lt's very romantic.


00:25:35.826 --> 00:25:36.993
lsn't it, Joe?


00:25:38.826 --> 00:25:43.163
Well, it is. You two were,
like, total lovebirds, and then...


00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:48.428
Well, it's just so obvious now


00:25:48.492 --> 00:25:50.760
because the women
that you choose to be around


00:25:50.826 --> 00:25:55.430
are, like, 360 degrees
in the other direction.


00:25:55.492 --> 00:25:57.427
They're, like--


00:25:57.492 --> 00:25:58.492
lt's 180.


00:25:59.993 --> 00:26:01.060
What?


00:26:01.126 --> 00:26:03.561
lt's 180.


00:26:03.626 --> 00:26:05.761
But it's interesting because inadvertently,
you stumbled on--


00:26:05.826 --> 00:26:07.460
Joe!


00:26:07.526 --> 00:26:08.593
Yeah?


00:26:08.659 --> 00:26:11.194
Joe Deacks. How you doing?


00:26:11.259 --> 00:26:13.427
- Okay.
- Hi, girls. How are you?


00:26:13.492 --> 00:26:14.759
Good.


00:26:14.826 --> 00:26:16.294
lt's been a few years, huh?


00:26:16.359 --> 00:26:17.426
These are my daughters.


00:26:17.492 --> 00:26:19.126
l know.


00:26:32.492 --> 00:26:34.427
Dad?


00:26:38.160 --> 00:26:41.296
Come on, Dad.


00:26:42.993 --> 00:26:45.295
lt's Mitch. He worked for you
for a long time.


00:26:45.359 --> 00:26:48.562
Remember? He bought all your equipment.


00:26:54.459 --> 00:26:55.760
Still runs good, too.


00:26:55.826 --> 00:26:57.227
That's my boy Ray over there.


00:27:03.826 --> 00:27:05.093
All right.


00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:08.763
Well, come by and see me sometime.


00:27:08.826 --> 00:27:11.862
You can visit the old tractor
and the backhoe


00:27:11.926 --> 00:27:13.794
and help me give them a lube job.


00:27:13.859 --> 00:27:15.527
All right. Sounds good.


00:27:15.592 --> 00:27:17.060
Here, Joe. Why don't you--
You should eat now.


00:27:17.126 --> 00:27:19.428
- Good to see you. Yes, sir.
- Okay.


00:27:19.492 --> 00:27:20.593
See you, girls. Be good.


00:27:20.659 --> 00:27:21.826
Bye, Mitch.


00:27:33.160 --> 00:27:34.761
You did?


00:27:34.826 --> 00:27:37.762
Well, you can show me
when l get back tomorrow night.


00:27:37.826 --> 00:27:42.564
Will you have Daddy call me
as soon as he's done with his client?


00:27:42.626 --> 00:27:44.127
- Auntie Jayne sends kisses.
- Hi.


00:27:45.993 --> 00:27:47.027
Okay, baby.


00:27:47.093 --> 00:27:48.093
Bye.


00:27:51.826 --> 00:27:53.093
We need to deal with Joe.


00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:54.594
He's fine. He's napping.


00:27:54.659 --> 00:27:56.360
l mean long-term.


00:28:11.160 --> 00:28:12.094
So--


00:28:12.160 --> 00:28:13.928
Nursing home.


00:28:13.993 --> 00:28:16.261
l can't do it. My plate's full.


00:28:16.325 --> 00:28:18.760
What about me? What about my plate?


00:28:18.826 --> 00:28:21.094
Well, that's an idea.


00:28:21.160 --> 00:28:23.662
He could come live
with Jackson and me.


00:28:23.726 --> 00:28:26.261
He's going to need
full-time nursing care.


00:28:26.325 --> 00:28:28.560
Okay.


00:28:30.160 --> 00:28:34.397
Well, then, by all means, he's all yours.


00:28:58.826 --> 00:29:02.095
So we'll go through
Mommy's stum, finally.


00:29:02.160 --> 00:29:04.428
lt's all yard sale junk anyway.


00:29:04.492 --> 00:29:05.693
No, it's not.


00:29:05.759 --> 00:29:07.894
Some of this is Americana.


00:29:07.959 --> 00:29:10.227
Call it whatever the fuck you want.
Leave me some.


00:29:17.192 --> 00:29:18.793
lt's her.


00:29:37.160 --> 00:29:39.095
Shelly.


00:29:39.160 --> 00:29:40.427
Hi.


00:29:40.492 --> 00:29:41.826
l'm going to go see Joe.


00:29:42.826 --> 00:29:43.760
He's resting.


00:29:43.826 --> 00:29:45.561
Yeah, let's just let him sleep.


00:29:45.626 --> 00:29:46.760
Yeah.


00:29:46.826 --> 00:29:49.094
You can take om your coat
and stay a while.


00:29:49.160 --> 00:29:50.661
Yeah. Take it om.


00:29:54.160 --> 00:29:58.097
We haven't had a chance to chat and--
Would you like a beer?


00:29:58.160 --> 00:29:59.661
l'll get it.


00:30:02.826 --> 00:30:04.761
Can you believe her nerve?


00:30:04.826 --> 00:30:07.328
At least somebody's
getting some use out of it.


00:30:10.659 --> 00:30:13.828
You don't have a single sentimental
bone in your body.


00:30:17.492 --> 00:30:19.894
Did you see her nails?


00:30:19.959 --> 00:30:22.961
Hey, Shelly, why don't you
come on in and join us?


00:30:31.160 --> 00:30:32.261
Tough day?


00:30:35.225 --> 00:30:37.293
Yeah.


00:30:39.826 --> 00:30:44.597
You've been at the hospital all this time?


00:30:44.659 --> 00:30:46.093
Yeah.


00:30:46.160 --> 00:30:47.227
Wow.


00:30:47.292 --> 00:30:49.761
- That's some shift.
- Yeah.


00:30:49.826 --> 00:30:51.093
Let's think about it. Let's see--


00:30:51.160 --> 00:30:53.028
That's like, what, 20 hours?


00:31:00.492 --> 00:31:03.027
So...


00:31:03.093 --> 00:31:06.463
what hospital are you at?


00:31:07.826 --> 00:31:08.893
Today?


00:31:11.160 --> 00:31:12.194
Mount--


00:31:13.659 --> 00:31:16.061
Sinai.


00:31:18.659 --> 00:31:21.595
You work at dimerent ones?


00:31:24.325 --> 00:31:26.060
You're kind of--
You know what it sounds like?


00:31:26.126 --> 00:31:27.961
Like how Mommy used to do,


00:31:28.026 --> 00:31:30.428
where she used to fill in
at schools. Bless you.


00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:35.897
You know, at dimerent--


00:31:41.826 --> 00:31:43.394
so how much schooling--


00:31:47.160 --> 00:31:49.095
l think she hasn't really dealt with...


00:31:53.325 --> 00:31:54.592
l'm going to kill you.


00:32:03.959 --> 00:32:06.594
You don't at least feel sorry for him?


00:32:06.659 --> 00:32:09.094
Why should l? He's had a long life,


00:32:09.160 --> 00:32:12.096
and he's lived it
exactly as he's wanted to.


00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:14.095
That's not really true.


00:32:14.160 --> 00:32:17.429
Remember? He was going to have
this great singing career,


00:32:17.492 --> 00:32:20.428
and then he had to give it up
when his voice changed.


00:32:20.492 --> 00:32:23.094
He fucked the booker's wife.


00:32:23.160 --> 00:32:27.063
That's why his career ended.


00:32:27.126 --> 00:32:30.829
Sorry. l didn't realize
you still believed that old story.


00:32:32.492 --> 00:32:34.994
How come l don't know this?


00:32:36.492 --> 00:32:37.826
Because you don't want to.


00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:45.029
He couldn't have been more than 14.


00:33:03.425 --> 00:33:06.427
The chicken was in the oven
for over an hour,


00:33:06.492 --> 00:33:09.428
so l'm pretty sure it's dead.


00:33:09.492 --> 00:33:10.593
lt's delicious.


00:33:10.659 --> 00:33:11.693
You won't be needing--


00:33:17.160 --> 00:33:18.160
That's funny.


00:33:21.160 --> 00:33:22.928
You know, my sister's
in medicine, too, sort of.


00:33:22.993 --> 00:33:25.595
Did she tell you?


00:33:25.659 --> 00:33:28.928
She works for the...


00:33:31.160 --> 00:33:33.562
Foundation for Environmental Defense.


00:33:35.926 --> 00:33:38.094
What do they have you doing over there?


00:33:38.160 --> 00:33:41.263
l study and evaluate water quality.


00:33:41.325 --> 00:33:43.427
She has to travel all over the world.


00:33:43.492 --> 00:33:45.760
So you girls aren't stripping anymore?


00:33:45.826 --> 00:33:47.427
Joe.


00:33:47.492 --> 00:33:50.094
Dad, l mean-- You have to tell
everyone our business?


00:33:50.160 --> 00:33:51.728
That's nothing to be ashamed of.


00:33:51.792 --> 00:33:53.260
- It was one summer.
- Yeah, for money.


00:33:53.325 --> 00:33:54.592
Yeah, no shit.


00:33:57.993 --> 00:33:59.461
Joe told me you married a rich guy.


00:33:59.526 --> 00:34:03.129
Yeah. So?


00:34:03.192 --> 00:34:04.393
What's he do?


00:34:06.225 --> 00:34:07.626
His dad--


00:34:11.160 --> 00:34:16.598
was a big, famous artist,
and he-- he deals with that.


00:34:19.492 --> 00:34:20.526
What--


00:34:21.959 --> 00:34:23.794
What kind of art?


00:34:23.859 --> 00:34:25.060
Right?


00:34:25.126 --> 00:34:27.161
Contemporary.


00:34:31.826 --> 00:34:33.761
lt's kind of hard to explain.


00:34:33.826 --> 00:34:36.528
lt's-- If you look at it--


00:34:44.160 --> 00:34:45.361
lf you look at it,


00:34:45.425 --> 00:34:47.426
you don't really understand it.


00:34:47.492 --> 00:34:52.630
You have to know a lot
about other kinds of art


00:34:52.692 --> 00:34:56.762
in order to...to get it.


00:34:56.826 --> 00:35:01.463
Otherwise, it's just, like-- it's--


00:35:01.526 --> 00:35:03.194
You sure got the body
to marry a rich guy.


00:35:05.160 --> 00:35:06.227
Thanks.


00:35:09.459 --> 00:35:10.793
You make me sound like a gold digger.


00:35:11.826 --> 00:35:13.861
What are you laughing at?


00:35:13.926 --> 00:35:16.428
You, too. You got a rocking body.


00:35:16.492 --> 00:35:17.492
How come you didn't?


00:35:17.559 --> 00:35:19.894
Because she fell in love with a faggot.


00:35:21.826 --> 00:35:23.260
He likes to call him that


00:35:23.325 --> 00:35:26.161
because Laurent enjoys
cooking and gardening.


00:35:26.225 --> 00:35:30.095
And because he waves
his hands around like a faggot.


00:35:30.160 --> 00:35:31.394
But he's not.


00:35:31.459 --> 00:35:33.360
Not at all.


00:35:34.826 --> 00:35:37.261
He's a masseur.


00:35:41.926 --> 00:35:43.227
Wow.


00:35:44.893 --> 00:35:48.496
Well, it's good to have
all my girls around...


00:35:50.093 --> 00:35:51.527
together.


00:36:18.160 --> 00:36:20.795
l'm going to go to work.


00:36:25.160 --> 00:36:26.160
Bye, baby.


00:36:27.626 --> 00:36:28.626
Love you.


00:36:32.826 --> 00:36:34.093
She's had two kids,


00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:36.262
but she's still real tight.


00:36:37.826 --> 00:36:38.726
Joe.


00:36:40.492 --> 00:36:42.360
Can't even use this.


00:36:42.425 --> 00:36:44.460
Hey, you forgot something.


00:36:50.659 --> 00:36:53.161
You'll be needing that,
right? For work.


00:37:46.160 --> 00:37:47.961
l'm a king bee


00:37:49.826 --> 00:37:51.160
That's good.


00:37:51.225 --> 00:37:53.760
Be my queen bee


00:37:53.826 --> 00:37:55.827
Be my queen


00:37:57.259 --> 00:38:00.161
Queen bee


00:38:00.225 --> 00:38:01.926
Be my queen


00:38:06.492 --> 00:38:10.429
l'm a king bee


00:38:10.492 --> 00:38:14.495
And l'm buzzing around your hive


00:38:19.492 --> 00:38:23.095
l'll put you back, baby


00:38:23.160 --> 00:38:28.865
lf you let me come inside


00:38:28.926 --> 00:38:31.261
Yeah.


00:38:31.325 --> 00:38:33.760
Jackson's coming.


00:38:33.826 --> 00:38:35.594
Here?


00:38:35.659 --> 00:38:37.160
Yeah.


00:38:37.225 --> 00:38:39.360
Good. Good for him.


00:38:39.425 --> 00:38:42.528
Can buzz all night long


00:38:46.826 --> 00:38:48.661
Oh, my God. We can't sell the house.


00:38:51.160 --> 00:38:52.928
The buried treasure.


00:38:53.993 --> 00:38:55.427
Please, you're killing me.


00:38:55.492 --> 00:38:56.593
Why?


00:38:56.659 --> 00:38:58.227
There is no treasure.


00:39:01.160 --> 00:39:02.194
- Daddy--
- Stop.


00:39:02.259 --> 00:39:04.427
Stop idealizing this man.


00:39:04.492 --> 00:39:06.093
Daddy.


00:39:06.160 --> 00:39:07.361
Daddy!


00:39:07.425 --> 00:39:09.426
king...


00:39:09.492 --> 00:39:11.093
You know the treasure?


00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:12.427
The buried treasure?


00:39:12.492 --> 00:39:14.927
Quiet, pumpkin.


00:39:14.993 --> 00:39:16.427
Where did you bury it?


00:39:16.492 --> 00:39:18.093
You know where.


00:39:18.160 --> 00:39:20.028
But where? Exactly where?


00:39:20.093 --> 00:39:22.161
What are you, the FBl?


00:39:36.993 --> 00:39:38.761
lt's gold.


00:39:38.826 --> 00:39:43.030
Some temple treasure.


00:39:43.093 --> 00:39:47.030
How many times have you
seen this clunker?


00:39:47.093 --> 00:39:51.096
Death, the eternal punishment...


00:39:51.160 --> 00:39:57.099
for anyone who opens this casket.


00:39:57.160 --> 00:40:01.097
ln the name of Amon-Ra,


00:40:01.160 --> 00:40:04.096
the king of the gods.


00:40:04.160 --> 00:40:07.096
Good heavens, what a terrible curse.


00:40:07.160 --> 00:40:08.761
Well, let's see what's inside.


00:40:08.826 --> 00:40:12.429
Wait. You'll break the curse.


00:40:12.492 --> 00:40:16.662
We recognize your mastery
of the occult sciences, Miller...


00:40:29.160 --> 00:40:31.996
So sad she never got to go there.


00:40:34.659 --> 00:40:36.394
Anywhere.


00:40:38.893 --> 00:40:42.429
Mallory. What a sweetie.


00:40:42.492 --> 00:40:46.095
But she'd die of fright on an airplane.


00:40:46.160 --> 00:40:47.427
l don't think so.


00:40:47.492 --> 00:40:52.430
She talked a good game,
but she'd never go.


00:40:52.492 --> 00:40:54.327
She had her little cowboy, didn't she?


00:40:54.392 --> 00:40:55.893
Yeah.


00:42:03.492 --> 00:42:05.026
Wear this around your neck.


00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:13.997
Want me to turn the TV om
and go to bed?


00:42:15.492 --> 00:42:17.160
No, l'll wait up for your mother.


00:42:33.160 --> 00:42:38.098
Death, in the name of Amon-Ra,


00:42:38.160 --> 00:42:40.195
the king of the gods.


00:43:34.959 --> 00:43:39.096
$75, $175,,


00:43:39.160 --> 00:43:43.764
$2,300.


00:43:43.826 --> 00:43:45.627
Oh, Daddy.


00:44:12.826 --> 00:44:13.860
Hello.


00:44:13.926 --> 00:44:15.093
Oh, shit.


00:44:15.160 --> 00:44:17.061
Oh, God. You scared
the shit out of me, girl.


00:44:17.126 --> 00:44:19.428
lt's 4:30 in the morning.


00:44:22.160 --> 00:44:23.928
You got a big problem with me,
don't you?


00:44:23.993 --> 00:44:25.728
Yeah, you bet l do, girl.


00:44:33.093 --> 00:44:35.528
You're using my father.


00:44:35.592 --> 00:44:37.894
That's right. Yeah.


00:44:45.160 --> 00:44:46.728
Well, it's not nice.


00:44:46.792 --> 00:44:50.095
l like your father.


00:44:50.160 --> 00:44:52.495
He is a total freak.


00:44:57.492 --> 00:44:58.593
What are you after?


00:45:01.659 --> 00:45:03.927
What do you think l'm after?


00:45:03.993 --> 00:45:06.595
Money.


00:45:06.659 --> 00:45:08.093
And a place to live.


00:45:08.160 --> 00:45:09.394
Yeah.


00:45:09.459 --> 00:45:12.428
Same as everyone else.


00:45:12.492 --> 00:45:14.393
Only you're stealing it.


00:45:15.626 --> 00:45:17.394
Here. Look. Right here.


00:45:17.459 --> 00:45:18.393
Stop waving that in my face.


00:45:18.459 --> 00:45:20.427
lt is a forged check, addressed--


00:45:20.492 --> 00:45:24.996
written out to the order
of Shelly Poppy for $20.


00:45:26.826 --> 00:45:30.029
Well, these others are for more.


00:45:30.093 --> 00:45:34.096
Okay, great.
So l ask your father for money.


00:45:34.160 --> 00:45:36.762
Yeah, and sometimes he gives it to me.


00:45:36.826 --> 00:45:39.595
